@startuml
title TASK-260712-2lrpc0 - implemented cue and local-media contract

left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

package "Reviewed sources" {
  artifact "generate-recording-cue.go" as Generator
  artifact "pulsar-recording-cue.wav\nSHA-256 479b...30fd" as Cue
  artifact "capture-media-lifecycle-v1.json\n17 transitions" as Contract
}

package "macOS" {
  component "BuiltinRecordingCue\nexact loader" as MacLoader
  component "RecordingCueSequencer" as MacSequence
  component "CaptureMediaStore" as MacStore
  folder "Contents/Resources/Audio" as MacPackage
}

package "Windows" {
  component "LoadBuiltinRecordingCue\nexact loader" as WinLoader
  component "RecordingCueSequencer" as WinSequence
  component "CaptureMediaStore" as WinStore
  folder "Assets/Audio" as WinPackage
}

database "app-private/capture-media-v1" as Private {
  folder "partials\n*.partial.wav" as Partials
  folder "self-tests\n*.selftest.wav" as SelfTests
  folder "drafts\n*.draft.wav" as Drafts
}

Generator --> Cue : deterministic PCM16
Cue --> MacPackage : build verifies digest
Cue --> WinPackage : build verifies digest
MacPackage --> MacLoader
WinPackage --> WinLoader
Contract ..> MacSequence : conformance tests
Contract ..> WinSequence : conformance tests
Contract ..> MacStore : lifecycle
Contract ..> WinStore : lifecycle
MacStore --> Partials
MacStore --> SelfTests
MacStore --> Drafts
WinStore --> Partials
WinStore --> SelfTests
WinStore --> Drafts

note bottom of Private
Owner-only files and opaque 128-bit IDs.
No source filename, path, token, or media bytes enter logs.
Partials are never sendable. Valid durable drafts survive restart.
end note

@enduml
